  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 133 AM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nAbove-normal temperatures and generally dry conditions persist \nthrough the Long Term. West Texas and southeast New Mexico remain \nunder northeasterly flow aloft as the upper-level ridge meanders \nover the Great Basin and Four Corners regions. In this pattern, high \ntemperatures stay consistently in the mid-to-upper 90s across the \nregion, with 100 degree temperatures confined mainly to the river \nvalleys. Lows in the mid 70s will also be commonplace (mid-to-upper \n60s in usual cool spots). As far as rain chances go, most of the \narea looks to remain dry through at least early next week. The \nexception will be in and around the higher terrain, particularly the \nDavis Mountains, where low (10-20%) shower and storm chances stick \naround most days thanks largely to upslope flow. \n\nSprang",
